        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/secure-renegotiation-enforcement-rfc-5746",
          "ruleIndex": 12,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "secure renegotiation enforcement (RFC 5746) — Requires further review: TLS 1.2 renegotiation handling\n\nThe library stores its own Finished verify_data (tlse.c:9357-9368) and sends a renegotiation_info extension (0xff01) when renegotiating (tlse.c:7276-7284), but the extension parser has no case for 0xff01 and no code compares a received renegotiation_info against the stored verify_data. With TLS_ACCEPT_SECURE_RENEGOTIATION enabled, a HelloRequest triggers _private_tls_reset_context and a new ClientHello (tlse.c:9900-9912) without enforcing RFC 5746. Not demonstrated dynamically; the option is not enabled by default."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "TLS 1.2 renegotiation handling"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "needs_follow_up",
              "risk_area": "secure renegotiation enforcement (RFC 5746)",
              "surface": "TLS 1.2 renegotiation handling",
              "recorded_by": "TLS 1.3, State Machine &amp; STUN/SRTP Auditor",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/protocol-downgrade-protection",
          "ruleIndex": 13,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "protocol downgrade protection — Requires further review: TLS 1.3 downgrade protection (server_random DOWNGRD sentinel)\n\nServer emits the RFC 8446 sentinel (DOWNGRD\\x01 / DOWNGRD\\x00) at tlse.c:7098-7102, but no client code ever compares the received server_random against it: the only sentinel the client checks is the HelloRetryRequest magic value (tlse.c:8218). A client built with TLS_LEGACY_SUPPORT therefore accepts a TLS 1.2 ServerHello after offering 1.3 without noticing the downgrade (tlse.c:8203-8214). Not dynamically demonstrated; impact depends on the legacy build option and on which TLS 1.2 cipher is then selected."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "TLS 1.3 downgrade protection (server_random DOWNGRD sentinel)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
