        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/error-handling-partial-reads-return-code-checks",
          "ruleIndex": 14,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "error handling, partial reads, return-code checks — No issue identified: tls_read / tls_write / tls_pending / tls_consume_stream API layer\n\nReviewed the blocking layer: tls_read returns 0 or the copied byte count and never a negative length, tls_write returns len or a negative error from _private_tls_write_packet, and tls_consume_stream returns a negative err_flag for any parse failure while clearing the message buffer. WANT_READ/WANT_WRITE concepts do not exist (the layer is non-blocking by buffer). Minor robustness note: tls_pending dereferences context without a NULL check."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "tls_read / tls_write / tls_pending / tls_consume_stream API layer"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
