        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/null-dereference-api-ordering",
          "ruleIndex": 15,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "NULL dereference / API ordering — Requires further review: tls_peerconnection_remote_credentials\n\nConfirmed crash: tls_peerconnection_remote_credentials dereferences channel->context->dtls_data (tlse.c:13790) without checking channel->context, and tls_peerconnection_context() does not create a context. Calling the credential setter before tls_peerconnection_connect() produces a NULL-pointer read and SEGV under ASan. Not filed as a vulnerability: the trigger is application call ordering, not remote input, and the library documents no ordering requirement. Recommended hardening: return TLS_GENERIC_ERROR when channel->context is NULL."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "tls_peerconnection_remote_credentials"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
