        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/remote-certificate-fingerprint-verification",
          "ruleIndex": 17,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "remote certificate fingerprint verification — Ruled out: tls_peerconnection_* DTLS certificate fingerprint check\n\nNamed control: the fingerprint comparison at tlse.c:8743 does strcmp(buffer_data, context->dtls_data->remote_fingerprint) for every parsed certificate when a remote fingerprint was set, and returns TLS_UNSUPPORTED_CERTIFICATE on mismatch, which is fatal to the handshake. The computed value is \"AA:BB:...\" uppercase SHA-256 of the DER. Reviewed the formatting loop: the typo `buf_len -= 2` (instead of buf_len_) cannot overflow the 100-byte buffer because the loop writes at most 95 characters. Residual note: the check is skipped entirely when the application never calls tls_peerconnection_remote_credentials, which is the documented WebRTC model (fingerprint is the only authentication) but leaves authentication to the caller."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "tls_peerconnection_* DTLS certificate fingerprint check"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
