              "risk_area": "remote certificate fingerprint verification",
              "surface": "tls_peerconnection_* DTLS certificate fingerprint check",
              "recorded_by": "TLS 1.3, State Machine &amp; STUN/SRTP Auditor",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/parameter-selection-outside-the-client-offer",
          "ruleIndex": 18,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "parameter selection outside the client offer — No issue identified: ServerHello version/cipher/group acceptance\n\nReviewed the client cipher and version gates: a ServerHello version is rejected when it exceeds the offer (VERSION_SUPPORTED plus the downgrade block), supported_versions is only honoured when the client offered TLS 1.3 (tlse.c:8500-8512), the selected cipher is validated with tls_cipher_supported after extensions are parsed (tlse.c:8576) and unknown/unsupported ciphers return TLS_NO_COMMON_CIPHER, and the key_share group is parsed by _private_tls_parse_key_share which rejects unknown groups with TLS_NO_COMMON_CIPHER. A server may select a group the client did not offer (e.g. P-384 after offering P-256), which is a protocol-violation interop issue rather than a security weakness."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "ServerHello version/cipher/group acceptance"
                }
