        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/session-resumption-ticket-handling",
          "ruleIndex": 19,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "session resumption / ticket handling — No issue identified: Session resumption and NewSessionTicket handling\n\nTLS 1.3 NewSessionTicket handling (case 0x04, tlse.c:9960-9978) validates the ticket and extensions lengths against the payload with CHECK_SIZE and rejects a zero-length ticket. TLS 1.2 session resumption is limited to recording the session_id returned in ServerHello (tlse.c:8232-8243); the state machine still expects the full handshake, so no abbreviated/resumed path is reachable that would skip key establishment. TLS 1.3 session tickets are not used to build a PSK (no pre_shared_key is ever sent), so there is no resumption path at all in 1.3."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
