        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/alert-and-close-notify-handling-truncation-detection",
          "ruleIndex": 20,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "alert and close-notify handling / truncation detection — No issue identified: Alert and close_notify processing\n\nAlert handling (tlse.c:10892-10908) sets critical_error for a fatal alert and peerclosed for close_notify, and tls_consume_stream stops processing once peerclosed. Observed weakness, low impact: close_notify only sets peerclosed, not critical_error, so tls_write still succeeds on a half-closed connection, and a transport close without close_notify is indistinguishable from a clean close at the library boundary (the application must check peerclosed to detect truncation)."
          },
          "locations": [
