          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Stack exhaustion / resource consumption — Requires further review: tls_parse_payload stack scratch buffer (tlse.c:9802)\n\n`unsigned char local_buffer[DTLS_MAX_FRAGMENT_SIZE + 12]` at tlse.c:9802 is a 262,156-byte stack frame in tls_parse_payload, allocated on every handshake message including non-DTLS and unfragmented ones. Not attacker-controlled by itself, so no overflow is reachable from it, but it will fault on threads with a small/default stack. Deployment-dependent, so unproven here."
          },
