        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/attacker-controlled-length-feeding-memcpy",
          "ruleIndex": 22,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Attacker-controlled length feeding memcpy — Ruled out: tls_parse_hello extension parsers (SNI, ALPN, session id, retry cookie)\n\nSNI (tlse.c:8378) copies into `TLS_MALLOC(sni_host_len + 1)` with source bounded by `CHECK_SIZE(sni_host_len, extension_len - 5)` at tlse.c:8374; session id (tlse.c:8237) guarded by `session_len <= TLS_MAX_SESSION_ID` at tlse.c:8236; retrycookie (tlse.c:8360) copies into `TLS_MALLOC(extension_len - 2)` sized at tlse.c:8356; ALPN (tlse.c:8445, tlse.c:9792) copies into `TLS_MALLOC(size + 1)` and tlse.c:9790 forces `extensionsize == protocolsize + 3`. Every destination is allocated from the same length that is copied, on the attacker-reachable path."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "tls_parse_hello extension parsers (SNI, ALPN, session id, retry cookie)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Attacker-controlled length feeding memcpy",
              "surface": "tls_parse_hello extension parsers (SNI, ALPN, session id, retry cookie)",
              "recorded_by": "Static Baseline &amp; Source Map",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/integer-width-underflow-in-record-length-arithmetic",
          "ruleIndex": 23,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Integer/width underflow in record length arithmetic — Ruled out: tls_parse_message decrypt length arithmetic (tlse.c:10480-10760)\n\nThe AEAD and ChaCha20-Poly1305 branches compute `pt_length = length - 8 - TLS_GCM_TAG_LEN` / `length - POLY1305_TAGLEN` from an unsigned-short record length; both branches reject the underflow with an explicit `if (pt_length < 0)` before calling gcm_process / chacha_encrypt_bytes (tlse.c:10565 and tlse.c:10634). The 8-byte explicit-nonce read at tlse.c:10562 is guarded by `length < 8` at tlse.c:10487. The CBC branch (tlse.c:10700+) keys `padding_index` off a signed int and gates on `padding_index > 0`, so a padding value larger than the record falls through rather than indexing backwards."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "tls_parse_message decrypt length arithmetic (tlse.c:10480-10760)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Integer/width underflow in record length arithmetic",
              "surface": "tls_parse_message decrypt length arithmetic (tlse.c:10480-10760)",
              "recorded_by": "Static Baseline &amp; Source Map",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/integer-overflow-in-buffer-growth",
          "ruleIndex": 24,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Integer overflow in buffer growth — Requires further review: tls_packet_append growth arithmetic (tlse.c:5305-5330)\n\ntlse.c:5309-5325 computes `new_len = packet->len + len` as unsigned int with no overflow check; if it wrapped, `new_len <= packet->size` would skip the realloc and the following `memcpy(packet->buf + packet->len, buf, len)` would write `len` bytes into the old buffer. Grepped all 26 call sites: every one passes either a compile-time constant, a crypto output length (<= 512), or a context field sized by a length that was itself already bounded (session_size, retrycookielength, verify_len, sni_len). No caller was found that can pass an attacker-influenced length near 2^32, so the wrap is not demonstrably reachable, but it is also not defended by any call-site invariant."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "tls_packet_append growth arithmetic (tlse.c:5305-5330)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "needs_follow_up",
              "risk_area": "Integer overflow in buffer growth",
              "surface": "tls_packet_append growth arithmetic (tlse.c:5305-5330)",
              "recorded_by": "Static Baseline &amp; Source Map",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/deserialization-length-validation-bypass",
          "ruleIndex": 25,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Deserialization length validation bypass — Ruled out: tls_import_context length-prefixed deserialization (tlse.c:12757-13000)\n\nCandidate was \"the `TLS_IMPORT_CHECK_SIZE` subtraction wraps and lets an oversized length through\". Disproved by reading the full expansion at tlse.c:788: `if (((size) > (buf_size - buf_pos)) || ((buf_pos) > (buf_size)))`. In the wrap case `buf_pos > buf_size`, `buf_size - buf_pos` becomes a value near 2^32, so the first comparison is false for any `unsigned int` size, and the second disjunct `buf_pos > buf_size` then fires and returns NULL after tls_destroy_context. When `buf_pos <= buf_size` there is no wrap and `size > buf_size - buf_pos` is the correct bound. Every element read in tls_import_context (tlse.c:12928 onwards) additionally allocates its destination with TLS_MALLOC of the very length it later copies, so the copies are self-consistent. This specific candidate is closed; the rest of tls_import_context (field-by-field semantic validation) was not exhaustively reviewed."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "tls_import_context length-prefixed deserialization (tlse.c:12757-13000)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "ruled_out",
              "risk_area": "Deserialization length validation bypass",
              "surface": "tls_import_context length-prefixed deserialization (tlse.c:12757-13000)",
              "recorded_by": "Static Baseline &amp; Source Map",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/unauthenticated-memory-exhaustion",
          "ruleIndex": 26,
          "kind": "open",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Unauthenticated memory exhaustion — Requires further review: Pre-auth per-connection buffer growth (message_buffer, handshakebuffer, cached_handshake)\n\nTwo unbounded per-connection accumulators were identified but not measured: `context->message_buffer_len += buf_len` then TLS_REALLOC at tlse.c:12460-12467 (record reassembly, no ceiling across records), `_private_tls_consume_handshake` accepting a 24-bit `messagesize` up to 16 MiB at tlse.c:10363-10389, and `cached_handshake` growing by TLS_REALLOC(..., new_len) at tlse.c:5510. All are pre-auth on a server. No memory ceiling or connection count limit is enforced in the library itself, so real impact depends on how an embedding server limits connections; not measured dynamically."
          },
          "locations": [
