              "coverage_outcome": "not_applicable",
              "risk_area": "Trust anchor loading from PEM",
              "surface": "tls_load_root_certificates / _private_tls_pem_decode (tlse.c:13487-13528, 4257)",
              "recorded_by": "X.509 &amp; ASN.1 Validation Auditor",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/silent-credential-load-failure-leading-to-a-malformed-serverkeyexchange-wrong-cipher-selection",
          "ruleIndex": 40,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "Silent credential-load failure leading to a malformed ServerKeyExchange / wrong cipher selection — No issue identified: Server handshake with absent or unloadable certificate and private key (tls_load_private_key, tls_build_certificate, tls_build_server_key_exchange)\n\nRoot-caused the earlier decode_error: openssl's default PKCS#8 EC key (\"BEGIN PRIVATE KEY\") is not parsed by tls_load_private_key (returns 0), and tls_is_ecdsa() then reports 0 for an ECDSA certificate, so the server sends an empty Certificate message plus an SKE with no signature; every conformant client aborts (decode_error). With the same key converted to SEC1 (\"BEGIN EC PRIVATE KEY\") the ECDHE-ECDSA handshake completes normally, so this is not a client interop bug. Security impact: none demonstrated - a server without a usable key cannot authenticate itself, so peers always fail the handshake and no bypass or credential exposure results. Robustness defects worth fixing separately: tls_load_private_key fails silently for PKCS#8 EC keys, the server does not abort when no certificate/private key is loaded, and an unsupported EC point format returns 0 (success) from tls_parse_server_key_exchange instead of an error."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "Server handshake with absent or unloadable certificate and private key (tls_load_private_key, tls_build_certificate, tls_build_server_key_exchange)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "strix": {
              "coverage_outcome": "no_issue_found",
              "risk_area": "Silent credential-load failure leading to a malformed ServerKeyExchange / wrong cipher selection",
              "surface": "Server handshake with absent or unloadable certificate and private key (tls_load_private_key, tls_build_certificate, tls_build_server_key_exchange)",
              "recorded_by": "mTLS Enforcement &amp; DTLS Replay Auditor",
              "source": "agent_reported"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/tls-1-2-server-authentication-bypass-unverified-serverkeyexchange-signature",
          "ruleIndex": 41,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "TLS 1.2 server authentication bypass (unverified ServerKeyExchange signature) — Ruled out: tls_parse_server_key_exchange (TLS 1.2 client path, tlse.c:8932-9203)\n\nNamed control: tls_parse_server_key_exchange builds client_random||server_random||params (tlse.c:9079-9084) and verifies the signature against the server certificate key, returning TLS_BROKEN_PACKET when it fails (tlse.c:9087-9099). Negative controls run in-process: flipping the last signature byte of a real SKE aborts the handshake for both ECDHE-RSA (consume -> -2, client established=-1) and ECDHE-ECDSA (-2), while the untampered flights complete and carry data; flipping a curve-id byte inside the SKE params is equally rejected. Handshake transcript binding also means any re-derived SKE breaks Finished. The tk observed decode_error after SKE was therefore the client correctly rejecting a malformed message, not a missing check."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "logicalLocations": [
                {
                  "fullyQualifiedName": "tls_parse_server_key_exchange (TLS 1.2 client path, tlse.c:8932-9203)"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
